  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 158 PM EDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nHigh temperatures in the mid to upper 70s will start off the long \nterm. Overnight lows will fall into the 50s with 40's likely in the \nhigher elevations of northern Georgia. By the time we get to \nThursday, rain chances for the CWA drop to nearly zero as the \nstationary front sinks into Florida. \n\nAs of the time writing this, the NHC is keeping an eye on a \ndisturbance off the Yucatan that they're giving a 80% chance of \ndevelopment in the next 7 days. All of the major models are \ndeveloping it into some kind of tropical system with landfall \nexpected somewhere along the Gulf coast east of NOLA. This would \nbring another round of wet weather to the area by next weekend.\n\nThe extent and intensity of this system is currently only \nspeculation and there is still a lot of uncertainty as to what and \nwhere this system will do. It's presence though will force the \nstationary front across northern Florida back north and it seems \nlikely that regardless of the track the storm takes, we'll likely \nhave another wet weekend. All interested parties should continue to \nmonitor the forecast as it evolves.",
